चिकीर्षु, उस्, उस्, उ, wishing to act, desiring or
intending to do or make or perform anything;
wishing to practice; desirous for.

चिक्क् चिक्क्, cl. 10. P. चिक्कयति, -यितुम्,
to feel pain; to give or inflict pain;
[cf. चक्क् and चुक्क्.]

चीक् चीक्, cl. 1. and 10. P. चीकति and
चीकयति, to endure, suffer, to be patient;
to be impatient; to touch.

चिक्किण चिक्किण, अस्, आ, अम्, glossy, shining,
smooth; slippery; bland, emollient; unctuous, greasy;
(आ), f. an excellent cow.

चिकित्वित्, ind., Ved. with intelligence, intelligently;
with deliberation, deliberately; (Sāy.) making known
(= ज्ञापयन्तीम् in Ṛg-veda

).
—चिकित्विन्-
मनस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, Ved. one whose mind is attentive;
coming from an intelligent mind, well considered;
(Sāy.) one who knows all hearts.
